      "message": "**File:** `util/focaltech/updater.cc` (Lines \\~163 \u0026 \\~168)\n\n**Corrected Snippet:**\n\n```c\n  while (len \u003e\u003d per_len) {\n    auto page_res \u003d\n        FtDownloadPage(device, downaddr, per_len, {p, static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(per_len)});\n    if (!page_res) return page_res;\n\n```\n\n*(Note: You will need to apply this exact same `static_cast` to line 168 as well)*\n\n* **Rationale:** C++ requires explicit type casting methods (`static_cast`, `const_cast`, `reinterpret_cast`) because they explicitly state the intent of the cast, enforce compiler checks, and are easy to `grep` for in a large codebase. Functional casts like `size_t(per_len)` or C-style casts like `(size_t)per_len` bypass these checks and are explicitly forbidden.  \n* **Google Style Guide:** [Casting](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Casting)",
